1.
Write an INNER JOIN query to fetch the order_id, customer_name, and product_name for all orders placed on your favorite food delivery app (imagine Swiggy or Zomato) using tables: Orders, Customers, and Products.
Answer:

SELECT 
    Orders.order_id,
    Customers.customer_name,
    Products.product_name
FROM Orders
INNER JOIN Customers
    ON Orders.customer_id = Customers.customer_id
INNER JOIN Products
    ON Orders.product_id = Products.product_id;

2.
Write a LEFT JOIN query to list all users from a Flipkart-style Users table and show their last order date from the Orders table, including users who have never placed an order.<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> Check for NULL values in the order date to identify users with no orders.</em>
Answer:

SELECT Users.user_id, Users.user_name, Orders.order_date
FROM Users
LEFT JOIN Orders
ON Users.user_id = Orders.user_id;

3.
Write a RIGHT JOIN query to display all products from a Myntra-style Products table and the name of the user who last bought each product from the Users table, including products that have never been purchased.
Answer:

SELECT Products.product_name, Users.user_name
FROM Users
RIGHT JOIN Products
ON Users.user_id = Products.user_id;

